CHOOSE-A-LICENSE

This file is a placeholder. CI fails while the marker on the first line is
still here, so a repository cannot reach `main` without a license. That is
deliberate: eight of the eleven repositories that existed before this template
had none, and none of them was left unlicensed on purpose — the omission was
simply never blocked by anything.

Replace this entire file with the full text of one of three licenses, chosen by
what the repository is. See `docs/CONVENTIONS.md` section 3.

  AGPL-3.0-or-later   software that can be run as a hosted service
  MIT                 tooling meant to be copied and adapted
  CC-BY-SA-4.0        documentation, not code

Two things are easy to get wrong here:

1. Copy the *full text*, not the short notice. A file containing only "This
   program is free software: you can redistribute it..." is the notice that
   belongs in source headers. The AGPL and the GPL both require their terms to
   accompany the work.

2. The `Copyright (c)` line names a holder that can enforce it:

     FreedzHost SASU        the harness and the fleet tooling
     Benoit Guarnaccia      the personal projects

   `Zordur` is the public identity in README.md and pyproject.toml authors. It
   is a signature, not a title.

Whatever you choose here must match what `pyproject.toml` declares in its
`license` field. CI checks that the two agree.
